<title>UK: Bankwest sets $150 mln five-year FRN. [CORRECTED 09:10 GMT]</title>
<headline>Bankwest sets $150 mln five-year FRN. [CORRECTED 09:10 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager Paribas.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANK OF WESTERN AUSTRALIA</p>
<p> AMT    $150 MLN	BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY    14.NOV.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     6.25 BP   PAY DATE    14.NOV.96</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A1	  ISS PRICE  99.99     FULL FEES   15 BP</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A	   REOFFER    99.99</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/AUS</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  AUSTRALIA TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    5 BP	SELL CONC  10 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>(Corrects issue and reoffer price from 99.94 to 99.99; Fees from 10 basis points to 15 bp; and selling fees from 5 basis points to 10 bp).</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
